WEBVTT

00:01:28.958 --> 00:01:31.226
at Weill Cornell Medicine
in New York City,

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:33.601
exactly to answer those questions.

00:01:33.625 --> 00:01:36.667
And tonight, I'm here with some answers.

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:42.476
So it turns out
our brains age differently,

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.208
and menopause plays
a key role here for women.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:50.476
Now most people think of the brain
as a kind of black box,

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.476
isolated from the rest of the body.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.601
But in reality, our brains
are in constant interaction

00:01:55.625 --> 00:01:56.893
with the rest of us.

00:01:56.917 --> 00:01:58.393
And perhaps surprisingly,

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:02.018
the interactions
with the reproductive system